WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.653
Weather planning begins with current official or otherwise approved sources appropriate to the location and operation.

00:00:07.653 --> 00:00:17.930
Review when the forecast was issued, the period it covers, and whether changing conditions are expected before, during, or after the mission.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:24.709
Check wind speed, gusts, direction, and expected changes at the surface and relevant altitude.

00:00:24.709 --> 00:00:31.924
A sheltered launch point may not represent conditions above trees, buildings, ridges, or shoreline terrain.

00:00:31.924 --> 00:00:40.015
Review precipitation probability, type, timing, visibility, cloud, temperature, humidity, and significant pressure or frontal changes where relevant.

00:00:40.015 --> 00:00:48.543
A percentage alone does not show whether rain will arrive during recovery or how intense it may be.

00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:50.511
Consider local effects.

00:00:50.511 --> 00:01:00.350
Terrain can channel wind, water can produce fog or spray, buildings can create turbulence, and sun-heated surfaces can generate unstable air.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:04.942
Prior site knowledge and an on-site check remain necessary.

00:01:04.942 --> 00:01:09.097
Forecast uncertainty should increase margin rather than confidence.

00:01:09.097 --> 00:01:19.811
When sources disagree or a front may arrive near recovery time, choose the more conservative interpretation and shorten, delay, or relocate the mission.

00:01:19.811 --> 00:01:27.464
Define go or no-go criteria before travel and before organizational pressure to complete the flight increases.

00:01:27.464 --> 00:01:35.992
Criteria should reflect current rules, aircraft and payload guidance, crew experience, route complexity, return margin, and data-quality needs.

00:01:35.992 --> 00:01:43.645
Plan alternatives: a later time, shorter route, different authorized platform, ground inspection, existing imagery, or rescheduling.

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:50.861
Document sources, assumptions, thresholds, and review time so the decision can be explained and updated.
